442
00:20:28,780 --> 00:20:30,840
Kotari loves her big brother more than anything.

443
00:20:33,220 --> 00:20:34,700
Something must be broken!

444
00:20:35,020 --> 00:20:37,320
There's no way those stupid measurements are right!

445
00:20:37,380 --> 00:20:37,860
Not true.

446
00:20:37,860 --> 00:20:40,560
There's nothing wrong with the measurements.

447
00:20:40,740 --> 00:20:43,540
Say the numbers are off or buy me a dozen cream puffs!

448
00:20:43,600 --> 00:20:44,620
My apologies, Shin.

449
00:20:45,220 --> 00:20:46,260
The measurements are wrong.

450
00:20:47,180 --> 00:20:47,660
Fine.

451
00:20:48,120 --> 00:20:48,600
Whatever.

452
00:20:48,600 --> 00:20:52,340
Anyway, you sure you're all right?

453
00:20:52,600 --> 00:20:54,860
Shouldn't you be resting or not kicking me?

454
00:20:54,960 --> 00:20:56,300
Don't have that kind of time.

455
00:20:56,700 --> 00:20:58,440
I have a long report to write, you know.

456
00:20:59,080 --> 00:21:00,900
We finally got our memories back.

457
00:21:01,240 --> 00:21:02,980
But they could always be erased again.

458
00:21:03,280 --> 00:21:06,620
If we want to make sure we can remember what really happened to us five years ago,

459
00:21:06,720 --> 00:21:10,700
then it would probably be smart to record the truth somewhere other than either one of our two heads.

460
00:21:11,340 --> 00:21:11,740
Understood.

461
00:21:12,420 --> 00:21:13,460
Don't work too hard.

462
00:21:13,660 --> 00:21:14,400
I won't.

463
00:21:15,620 --> 00:21:16,520
Oh, Shido.

464
00:21:16,520 --> 00:21:20,460
You know what you said before you sealed my spirit power?

465
00:21:20,780 --> 00:21:21,600
